  ('Pineapple', 'Ananas comosus', 'Bromeliaceae', 'uncommon', 'Bromelain lives in the core — the part most people throw away.'),
  ('Pear', 'Pyrus communis', 'Rosaceae', 'common', 'Gritty texture is stone cells plus pectin — gentle fiber in dessert clothing.'),
  ('Avocado', 'Persea americana', 'Lauraceae', 'uncommon', 'A fruit that eats like a fat — with more fiber per half than most salads.'),
  ('Fig', 'Ficus carica', 'Moraceae', 'rare', 'Ancient, jammy, and fiber-dense — fresh or dried, the seeds do the work.'),
  ('Cranberry', 'Vaccinium macrocarpon', 'Ericaceae', 'rare', 'A-type proanthocyanidins — the tart compounds behind its famous reputation.'),
  ('Date', 'Phoenix dactylifera', 'Arecaceae', 'uncommon', 'Nature''s caramel wrapped around real fiber — sweetness your microbes share.'),
  ('Basil', 'Ocimum basilicum', 'Lamiaceae', 'common', 'A handful of leaves is a legitimate plant — rosmarinic acid rides in the aroma.'),
  ('Parsley', 'Petroselinum crispum', 'Apiaceae', 'common', 'Not a garnish — one of the densest apigenin sources you can buy.'),
  ('Cilantro', 'Coriandrum sativum', 'Apiaceae', 'common', 'Love-it-or-soap — either way its leaf carries genuine phytochemical weight.'),
  ('Mint', 'Mentha spicata', 'Lamiaceae', 'common', 'Menthol freshness that turns water, yogurt, and salads into another plant point.'),
  ('Rosemary', 'Salvia rosmarinus', 'Lamiaceae', 'uncommon', 'Carnosic acid in needle form — a woody herb that survives every roast.'),
  ('Thyme', 'Thymus vulgaris', 'Lamiaceae', 'uncommon', 'Thymol in tiny leaves — a pinch across the week quietly adds up.'),
  ('Oregano', 'Origanum vulgare', 'Lamiaceae', 'uncommon', 'One of the highest polyphenol densities of any herb, dried or fresh.'),
  ('Cinnamon', 'Cinnamomum verum', 'Lauraceae', 'uncommon', 'Tree bark, technically — proanthocyanidins in dessert''s favorite spice.'),
  ('Nutmeg', 'Myristica fragrans', 'Myristicaceae', 'rare', 'A grating is plenty — warm spice with its own phytochemical signature.'),
  ('Cumin', 'Cuminum cyminum', 'Apiaceae', 'uncommon', 'The backbone of half the world''s spice blends — seeds with real polyphenol content.'),
  ('Black pepper', 'Piper nigrum', 'Piperaceae', 'common', 'Piperine — the everyday grind that helps other compounds (curcumin!) absorb.'),
  ('Sumac', 'Rhus coriaria', 'Anacardiaceae', 'legendary', 'The lemony crimson dust of Middle Eastern kitchens — a legendary polyphenol find.'),
  ('White mushroom', 'Agaricus bisporus', 'Agaricaceae', 'common', 'Fungi, not botanically a plant — but beta-glucans earn it a guide page and your 30.'),
  ('Shiitake mushroom', 'Lentinula edodes', 'Omphalotaceae', 'uncommon', 'Lentinan — a beta-glucan studied for decades — plus real umami depth.'),
  ('Oyster mushroom', 'Pleurotus ostreatus', 'Pleurotaceae', 'rare', 'Velvety, quick-cooking, and one of the richer beta-glucan mushrooms.'),
  ('Nori', 'Pyropia yezoensis', 'Bangiaceae', 'rare', 'The sushi wrap is a sea vegetable — minerals and fibers land plants can''t offer.'),
  ('Wakame', 'Undaria pinnatifida', 'Alariaceae', 'rare', 'The silky seaweed in miso soup — fucoidan, a fiber unique to the ocean.'),
  ('Kombu', 'Saccharina japonica', 'Laminariaceae', 'legendary', 'The umami kelp of dashi — glutamates plus ocean fibers, a legendary find.'),
  ('Kimchi', 'Brassica rapa (fermented)', 'Brassicaceae', 'rare', 'Cabbage transformed — live cultures plus the fiber it started with. A probiotic and a plant in one.'),
  ('Sauerkraut', 'Brassica oleracea (fermented)', 'Brassicaceae', 'uncommon', 'The simplest ferment there is: cabbage, salt, time. Choose the refrigerated kind — that''s where the cultures live.'),
  ('Miso', 'Glycine max (fermented)', 'Fabaceae', 'rare', 'Soybeans aged into savory depth — stir into warm (not boiling) broth to keep the cultures with you.'),
  ('Tempeh', 'Glycine max (fermented)', 'Fabaceae', 'rare', 'Whole soybeans bound by fungal fermentation — the fiber survives, unlike in most soy foods.'),
  ('Natto', 'Glycine max (fermented, Bacillus subtilis)', 'Fabaceae', 'legendary', 'The boldest ferment in the guide — sticky, pungent, and famous for vitamin K2. A legendary badge of honor.'),
  ('Kombucha', 'Camellia sinensis (fermented)', 'Theaceae', 'rare', 'Tea plus a culture — tangy, lightly fizzy, and a gentle way to add a fermented find to any day.')
on conflict (name) do update set
  scientific_name = excluded.scientific_name,
  plant_family = excluded.plant_family,
  rarity_tier = excluded.rarity_tier,
  description = excluded.description;

-- ---- foods — ON CONFLICT (canonical_name); plant_id via plants join --
